goals.en:
Upon the successful completion of this course, you will be able to:

Thesis (70%)
● develop a research project in which the research objectives are clearly and realistically formulated;
● formulate suitable research questions based on a review of literature;
● analyse appropriate primary (and secondary) data in light of recent scholarship;
● choose and employ the appropriate methodology to conduct the research project;
● integrate knowledge from various academic disciplines, recognising the fact that (current) complex challenges cannot be addressed by a single discipline;
● draw relevant conclusions in which the global-local connection is made visible;
● present your research project in a well-written academic thesis;
● communicate your research findings in an appropriate and understandable way.

Portfolio (30%)
● reflect on your own learning process and experiences;
● demonstrate your responsible leadership development;
● formulate your (personal and/or professional) mission and attitude towards lifelong learning;
● showcase your engagement as a global citizen;
● showcase your Capstone in the final week in an understandable way.

